                <l xml:id="m-1a40a68f-7d97-4e50-a3e7-e678ae8c5160" facs="#m-e78ed438-299b-4041-8961-3aa5fb31eab5" label="ambiguous">29</l><l xml:id="m-da8571d2-6d1c-4959-b087-9baba9740a8e" facs="#m-b6a971d8-8010-492f-963d-148e874ab00b" label="text-like">The Common Tones of the Mass.</l><l xml:id="m-15281790-727c-4fff-9c95-55f6d3175df5" facs="#m-09404d11-f099-4b08-9f5d-7215c24563f2" label="text-like">Examples of the Flex.</l><l xml:id="m-fd767810-126a-4c2f-a103-08d3e5bf4b2b" facs="#m-bf4f270c-54c9-4ac9-a4c3-b1517ec5a056" label="text-like">Examples of the Metrum.</l><l xml:id="m-341df3fd-58a0-4510-8a58-4d40c6d30a78" facs="#m-9d5288c5-5b27-4059-87fa-15890b87e545" label="lyrics-like">per- cé-pi¬ mus.</l><l xml:id="m-2d831584-e1a6-4acd-805f-96aefe8296a5" facs="#m-21b45987-081c-4e35-970d-e6cdea140d9b" label="lyrics-like">pi- e- tá- te pro- sé-que-re.</l><l xml:id="m-642c7656-a62a-4a81-97fa-29fc1d48cae7" facs="#m-68804847-d208-438b-b9e2-87877ee60429" label="lyrics-like">mo-ri-én- do con-féssi sunt. (A).</l><l xml:id="m-fdb284ee-3096-4e9b-8672-36cc5d3316af" facs="#m-2b886384-46e5-42f9-b7b9-6fc08c960340" label="lyrics-like">quae ré-cta sunt.</l><l xml:id="m-c0eebdaf-9ea1-4e75-a2dc-09b5c3bd1b2d" facs="#m-b7cbdc4b-0517-409e-9dd7-6b6edff53134" label="lyrics-like">or: con- fés-si sunt. (B).</l><l xml:id="m-c126c73e-96c0-4265-823d-f56ed062ff92" facs="#m-351ccaa6-0929-4c40-8962-0f25810e6c4f" label="text-like">In the body or the Prayer, the metrum comes first, then the flex. In the</l><l xml:id="m-9e48f316-e9e7-4eb7-a650-29e7fc6d9c8c" facs="#m-159df8a5-0041-4779-8ef0-d6a82c60e8db" label="text-like">conclusion, the opposite takes place. As a general rule, the metrum in the</l><l xml:id="m-2a5a400d-9cf7-4f98-aa43-a93c79415aad" facs="#m-4fae8d92-ba4d-41f6-9a53-8e3b1581f375" label="text-like">Prayer occurs at the colon; the fiex at the semi-colon, or. if there is no</l><l xml:id="m-5f9f6523-a39c-4ec4-8848-7a555f1eeffb" facs="#m-a95278dd-c730-459e-90be-64f455b30a35" label="text-like">semi-colon, at the first comma which follows the metrum when the sense</l><l xml:id="m-3ea2de71-97a3-4358-a7f2-b4da7b2763e8" facs="#m-f7146af7-d0f7-4328-8c95-dbb6c54ade91" label="text-like">cliows this being done.</l><l xml:id="m-5a057040-6f1d-433c-8ee5-01fd177ac665" facs="#m-d0bdcee4-5bc0-4c02-adb4-b750d3429768" label="lyrics-like">Attention is drawn to the fact that the words Jésum Christum Filium túum.</l><l xml:id="m-6864d5e7-0ada-49e0-abea-5e450f0fc4da" facs="#m-6f1e19d1-b8c2-445d-91f3-5fc0e55bede8" label="text-like">br which a prayer sometimes ends, (e. g. on the Feast and on the Octave or</l><l xml:id="m-763b3c6c-4eaf-4e71-9301-69f5a18bd3cf" facs="#m-792b2848-96e8-45c0-8037-8657efd77859" label="text-like">St. Stephen) form part of the body of the Prayer itself. The conclusion</l><l xml:id="m-a226caff-13c9-4a6c-9acc-4e964ba09d45" facs="#m-f495a0e8-000a-4ba7-a53a-c5a5e0077897" label="lyrics-like">therefore begins at the words Qui técum.</l><l xml:id="m-5b40dabb-585b-4e1a-a9ea-956915bdc86f" facs="#m-14c6bbed-8b1c-4873-92bc-b2e2b02fc07a" label="ambiguous">2. Ferial Tone.</l><l xml:id="m-4288637f-7e2a-49f3-a6ef-e561891d9ef0" facs="#m-aca2b834-46c3-4dd7-8522-2a4cb77d9b58" label="text-like">A) On Ferias, at Votive Masses which are not solemn. and at Masses for</l><l xml:id="m-0e6a5a09-a539-4611-8ae1-3b09216dff42" facs="#m-1ebc2767-1cf0-4f17-be31-51ba7ecbabb1" label="text-like">the Dead, the Prayers are sung in the ferial tone, that is recto tono from</l><l xml:id="m-f0d02608-93b2-434d-8119-fa5225a23c81" facs="#m-ba123cd8-cab4-45df-b7f0-488b4b6dd356" label="text-like">beginning to end, with only a slight pause in those places where the metrum</l><l xml:id="m-55eaa9c1-1dbd-48c4-884b-1e59d8c0f2dc" facs="#m-a2fa3e03-6b9e-4ea2-9fce-a8a7a86c0fc1" label="text-like">and the flex would have been used in the festal tone, and again at the ending.</l><l xml:id="m-2f1cc598-d08e-4e6b-ad09-11465e7bab72" facs="#m-14c3ed4b-d883-47e2-8bb1-d67cf3956ed3" label="text-like">B) However, there is another ferial tone which is used for the Prarers of</l><l xml:id="m-53112d48-bf61-40d6-8f69-ca0777641ab9" facs="#m-c8ab3afe-f4a1-40e0-950e-7f1c8c338146" label="text-like">the Litanies and of the Aspersion, and of other ceremonies of the same kind,</l><l xml:id="m-d4497b78-5153-48e8-9e00-80d0198a387a" facs="#m-840fd997-af55-4bd6-9d80-813d887b9c0e" label="text-like">such as the Washing of the feet, the Blessing of candles, of ashes, and or</l><l xml:id="m-9bdaeb8f-13f8-4959-b6f1-f4f6cea5e820" facs="#m-86c93d5f-4956-4c8e-8b81-c302c842ed21" label="ambiguous">palms.</l><l xml:id="m-bff276df-bfdd-4f05-b001-3e6b0d6348fc" facs="#m-7ec0df45-6157-43c5-a650-98bac511dd19" label="text-like">This second ferial tone is the same as the first ferial tone, except that,</l><l xml:id="m-a0eaf860-e0e8-4f27-89c0-2aed58bdb659" facs="#m-bca4a987-88e4-4eb0-a3d7-123f6c53b62b" label="text-like">at the end of the Prayer and at the end of the conclusion, the voice is lowered</l><l xml:id="m-bab644db-2608-4fbe-80f9-1f7bd8f74639" facs="#m-6d392d12-2c6b-4262-9577-ff56c8537d1b" label="text-like">a third — a minor third — for the fiex.</l><l xml:id="m-0e4e5c86-3450-4828-a867-3dce9a0a2253" facs="#m-d33b84be-0b1f-413e-8217-628765f42a28" label="text-like">The Prayers which precede the Mass of the Paschal Vigil, and the Pravers of</l><l xml:id="m-8153c2cb-39f0-4b25-92c7-ac334d42962f" facs="#m-4da6c538-2d23-4e2c-a52c-19cdf4723ca6" label="text-like">the Blessing of the Fonts are sung in the first ferial tone.</l><l xml:id="m-d7703269-3cdb-4d77-b296-066094da934c" facs="#m-b37955f5-a9c3-4fc3-b857-7d7c9feb3c76" label="lyrics-like">The Prayers which are preceded by Flectámus génua. are also sung in the</l><l xml:id="m-947bdf0a-d09d-47f8-98cd-8ebf81143a92" facs="#m-f1be4ba9-df9d-4e02-960e-ed50019fd8e5" label="ambiguous">first ferial tone.</l><l xml:id="m-99cb54a9-7e05-47c4-9ceb-1f9c01bac20f" facs="#m-f4c46899-a088-4c48-bd0b-6e5a5d35ce80" label="text-like">The Priest: The Deacon:</l><l xml:id="m-cb9c660a-6467-490b-a483-9637ff1d69c4" facs="#m-ab067596-c140-41cb-8e70-73e48684fcfc" label="text-like">The Sub-Deacon:</l><l xml:id="m-2af8acb4-8f74-48a8-94da-7c0ba178b934" facs="#m-64f4d41b-97d2-4181-a2ea-93791441b2ac" label="lyrics-like">Orémus. Flectámus génu-a. Levá-te. Praésta...</l><l xml:id="m-7cd4fe53-6f1f-47d1-9214-48bd3882b77c" facs="#m-dbc7b3d7-ab6c-4be0-86f6-3f72e8a8bf71" label="lyrics-like">The second ferial tone may be used for the Prayer Super pópulum. imnich is</l><l xml:id="m-baf2efe6-2f21-44da-9cec-cc78fed173a7" facs="#m-4600881a-2c56-4cd9-aa4a-9998635ecdce" label="text-like">said in Lent after the admonition:</l><l xml:id="m-419f39f4-63b5-47da-87ce-cccc3cf70ed0" facs="#m-7107272e-aaf3-4a80-9740-8eb403ea7ff7" label="lyrics-like">Humi-li-â-te cápi-ta véstra Dé-o.</l><l xml:id="m-de48ab81-3cf0-40da-8d81-43cd17ecceef" facs="#m-4446d0a5-660b-4395-8eea-e1c3970ed399" label="text-like">:In accordance with the decree of the Sacred Congregation of Rites, dated</l><l xml:id="m-38299034-7664-4ab2-880c-0d51d14d4497" facs="#m-173377bc-4b62-4137-b331-8cdc42cf15ad" label="text-like">July sth 1912. if a monosyllable or a Hebrew word occur in the Lessons or Versicles,</l><l xml:id="m-28097081-5d71-41de-96fc-4dde2e4d9096" facs="#m-ae90987d-149a-4562-a422-1c63e25226ee" label="lyrics-like">or ãt the mediant of the psalmis, it is permissible to modify the ending (R) or to kecp</l><l xml:id="m-1968033f-2888-438a-bea3-993fc4f36bb6" facs="#m-d37d7005-ff66-4786-beb2-428e060d5c10" label="text-like">the ordinary modulation (A).</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>